<i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="ג" data-order="3"></i> <i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="4"></i> <i data-commentator="Ateret Zekenim" data-label="♦" data-order="2"></i> One who rises early to plead before his Creator should intend [to pray at] the hours when the heavenly watches change—the end of the first third of the night, the end of the second third of <i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="6"></i> <i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="6"></i> the night, and the end <i data-commentator="Eshel Avraham" data-label="א" data-order="1"></i> of the night—for prayer offered at those times concerning the destruction [of the Temple] and the exile is desirable [before God].
